When SearXNG, ChromaDB, the ntfy server or a mail server disappears the app
keeps answering, just worse, and reminders silently stop. Nothing said why.

- src/service_health.py (stdlib, injectable probes): checks web search
  (SearXNG reachability or the provider API key), ChromaDB (when installed),
  ntfy (when reminders go there), the owner's enabled IMAP/SMTP servers and
  storage (readiness). Down is reported once per outage after two failed
  checks in a row, with the error and a fix; recovery is reported once.
- New scheduled task "Service Health" (check_services, :07/:37 every hour);
  silent (TaskNoop) when nothing changed.
- Daily brief gains a "Degraded services" section (from state, no probes).
- URLs go through check_outbound_url, redirects not followed, credentials
  and query strings redacted; email accounts owner-scoped.
- tests/test_service_health.py (11 tests), docs/service-health.md, ROADMAP.

